id: pm-linear-yyr9
title: A release that merges but fails to publish is abandoned by the next day's run
description: "Decide release computes the version from today's date and the existing tags, and the tag is pushed only after npm publish succeeds. If the protected release PR merges and publication then fails, main carries release metadata for a version that was never tagged or published. The next day's run sees the old latest tag, computes a new version from the new date, and commits it over the merged metadata, so the earlier version is silently skipped on npm. Needs a guard in Decide release that detects a committed-but-untagged version and resumes it rather than computing a new one."
type: Issue
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-09T13:46:47.559Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T22:59:51.369Z"
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "A failed publish after a merged release resumes the committed package version and release tag on later runs; Ordinary unreleased source changes receive a new date-based version and an unrelated manual version bump fails closed; A disposable Git fixture executes the actual workflow decision for both paths; The package release gate and exact-head CI and review gates pass before merge; If main has advanced past the release commit, the workflow refuses to publish or tag that pending version from a different source revision"
risk: high
blocked_reason: "Unmerged PR #126 awaits 100% coverage, resolution of two unprovable local merge receipts, and substantive configured final-head reviews; safe automatic recovery after newer main commits remains open."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T22:10:06.066Z",codex-sol,"Restart by codex-sol: preserved remote PR #126 and all existing bot replies/reactions were inspected. Branch is already current with origin/main. No new actionable unresolved inline finding is present. Retain documented coverage/health/publication blockers; rerun unchanged full CI gate with the host-wide flock. No merge, publish or item closure."
  "2026-10-02T22:25:25.986Z",codex-sol,"Restart: locked npm ci and release:check pass 219/219 tests, zero skips; configured index.ts coverage is 99.29% lines, 96.68% branches, 100% functions, with no separate statements dimension. PM-linked release-decision fixture tests pass, including later-head refusal, version mismatch, occupied tag, and nearest first-parent tag with skewed dates. Current worktree strict health with merge drivers passes; this fresh worktree lacks earlier clone-local merge receipts, so it does not reconcile the previously recorded pm-linear-unfa/4yle evidence. Coverage pm-linear-xw01 and substantive exact-head review remain blockers. No merge, publish, or close; release claim for orchestrator."
  "2026-10-02T22:41:25.559Z",codex-sol,"New exact-head feedback: CodeRabbit 4170348351 / Cubic 4170382743 request mainline annotated-tag coverage (valid); Cubic 4170382735 finds hardcoded repository name inconsistent with the release writer (valid). Add red fixtures and fix literal repository-prefix matching. Cubic 4170382715 asks to search older release commits after package.json advances; refuse because same-HEAD-only recovery is deliberate, and add a dependency-after-release refusal regression before outputs."
  "2026-10-02T22:59:50.273Z",codex-sol,"Review fixes: actual annotated mainline tag is selected as latest_tag; renamed repository containing a literal period resumes while the mismatched wildcard-like name refuses; dependency-followup package edit refuses before outputs. Annotated and renamed fixtures failed before their changes, then real workflow test and PM-linked command passed. Full locked release:check passes 219/219 with zero skips, measured index.ts 99.29 lines / 96.68 branches / 100 functions. Refuse scanning older release commits after main advances: this workflow requires original release HEAD and either failure message remains safely closed. Prior clone-local health receipts remain unreconciled; pm-linear-xw01 coverage remains open."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T16:29:55.004Z",codex,"2026-09-29 candidate: the disposable Git fixture failed on the previous workflow (new date tag instead of committed v2000.01.02), then passed after the decision resumed that tag. It also verifies a fresh feature gets a new version, later source commits preserve the pending version, and an unrelated manual version bump is refused. npm run release:check passed 219/219 tests, docstring 49/49 declarations across 8 files, audit 0 production vulnerabilities, and attestation gate 1/1 publish path; coverage measured 99.29% lines, 96.68% branches, 100% functions, below the requested 100% floor. pm health --strict-exit fails on two pre-existing merge receipts for pm-linear-unfa and pm-linear-4yle; pm merge reconcile --dry-run reports no_receipt_set_proves_snapshot for both, so neither was forced. Rollback: revert the workflow decision change before any release run; no registry or hosted state was changed by this candidate."
  "2026-09-29T16:31:15.876Z",codex,"Implementation PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/126 . Candidate code commit: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/commit/45ee8b3faf309f1d671f6f8009bc003635bc73f8 . Awaiting exact-head CI and configured bot review; leave unmerged while coverage and local strict-health blockers remain."
  "2026-09-29T16:40:30.460Z",codex,"Review reconciliation 2026-09-29: Greptile correctly found that a retry after later source commits could tag the newer HEAD for an already-published version. The candidate now refuses that state before emitting release outputs; automatic recovery across a newer main head requires a separate provenance-safe design. Greptile also identified two missing refusal cases; the disposable Git fixture now covers a conflicting tag on unrelated history and a release-subject/package-version mismatch. CodeRabbit correctly found tagger-clock order could select an older release; the workflow now selects the nearest reachable mainline release tag and a skewed-tagger-date fixture exercises it. None of these findings are treated as resolved until exact-head gates and re-review complete."
  "2026-09-29T16:50:20.378Z",codex,"Final review state for 4f71467426170c709240c2380e1ca35e943eaca9: Node 22 and 26 CI, CodeQL, local release:check 219/219, and Greptile re-review passed; Greptile explicitly marked both earlier findings addressed. CodeRabbit acknowledged the tag-selection fix but its requested full review was rate-limited for 47 minutes, and Sourcery reported an exhausted free weekly review budget. Neither is counted as substantive final-head approval. Measured source coverage remains 99.29% lines, 96.68% branches, 100% functions, with no separate statement metric. Local strict pm health still fails on two unprovable pre-existing merge receipts. PR #126 remains unmerged and no release or deployment occurred."
